WEBVTT

00:04.650 --> 00:07.740
Hey, hey, do you know those get sent out?

00:07.740 --> 00:08.530
What?

00:08.530 --> 00:11.030
Letters! From the dead!

00:11.030 --> 00:12.620
What's with that? How scary!

00:13.950 --> 00:16.910
Does a death god bring the letters to you saying, "You've got mail!"

00:16.910 --> 00:18.710
"May I have your signature?" or something?

00:19.000 --> 00:22.750
I heard it's true, a girl brings it to you!

00:28.470 --> 00:30.680
It's probably because this area is under redevelopment.

00:30.680 --> 00:33.680
We'll interrogate the folks nearby, if there are any.

00:33.680 --> 00:34.560
Noji-san!

00:34.560 --> 00:35.560
What is it?

00:55.200 --> 00:58.710
Really, humans are so infuriating!

00:59.210 --> 01:00.040
What do you mean?

01:00.370 --> 01:03.000
Why couldn't they say it while they were alive?

01:04.750 --> 01:07.840
There are things you cannot say until after your death.

01:11.010 --> 01:16.060
Shigofumi

01:22.560 --> 01:25.520
Shouta, your handwriting really is awful.

01:26.520 --> 01:28.900
For instance, how do you read this?

01:28.900 --> 01:29.900
Which one?

01:29.900 --> 01:30.950
This!

01:30.950 --> 01:31.700
"Su".

01:31.700 --> 01:32.740
"Su"?

01:32.860 --> 01:34.240
It's "Su".

01:34.370 --> 01:35.410
"Su"?!

01:35.530 --> 01:36.410
"Su".

01:39.410 --> 01:43.540
You're amazing! You can't do this, making up new letters!

01:43.540 --> 01:45.130
So strange!

01:46.250 --> 01:47.340
Hey, enough already!

01:48.760 --> 01:52.970
Hey, be more careful, that notebook is important to me.

01:52.970 --> 01:56.600
Gee, thanks for caring so much about me.

01:57.600 --> 02:02.480
Anyway, it's fine to work on your rocket,
but you should practice your penmanship too.

02:02.480 --> 02:03.730
Yeah, yeah.

02:03.730 --> 02:06.650
Miss student body president is strict, isn't she?

02:06.650 --> 02:10.940
That's right, everyone hates the president. It's rough.

02:11.860 --> 02:15.370
You're talking a lot today.
Usually, I'm the one doing all the talking.

02:15.370 --> 02:15.910
Really?

02:23.500 --> 02:25.170
A-Ayase!

02:25.750 --> 02:29.000
I... from a long time ago... I've...

02:35.180 --> 02:38.850
Yes, that's right, this is Ayase Asuna.

02:39.680 --> 02:41.430
How is my younger sister...?

02:43.600 --> 02:47.190
Yes, I understand, thank you.

02:54.780 --> 02:55.660
Ayase!

02:55.660 --> 02:58.530
They found my father's body.

03:01.080 --> 03:02.830
Kamome City
Police Station

03:13.170 --> 03:16.800
Ah, A-Ayase... I...

03:17.680 --> 03:21.510
The police are going to escort me home, so...

03:21.510 --> 03:22.720
I-I see.

03:24.230 --> 03:25.480
Sorry.

03:42.580 --> 03:44.080
Sending
Mail

03:42.580 --> 03:44.080
Ayase Asuna

03:42.580 --> 03:44.080
Subject

03:42.580 --> 03:44.080
Attachment

03:45.790 --> 03:49.710
<i>The body discovered was an unemployed man from Mikami Town.</i>

03:49.710 --> 03:52.170
<i>Mister Ayase Takezou, 45-years-old.</i>

03:52.170 --> 03:55.130
Ayase Takezou

03:52.170 --> 03:55.130
Male body discovered in Kamome City

03:53.170 --> 03:59.090
<i>Mister Ayase had been missing for the past four days, the family members put out a request for a search...</i>

04:19.610 --> 04:20.410
Sorry.

04:26.790 --> 04:27.870
Ayase?

04:30.630 --> 04:32.670
Kanaka, 0913.

04:32.670 --> 04:33.630
Understood!

04:33.630 --> 04:36.920
Ah! This isn't my fault! Really!

04:51.310 --> 04:53.110
Who are you?

04:53.110 --> 04:54.900
My name is Fumika.

04:54.900 --> 04:56.190
Fumika?

04:56.780 --> 04:59.740
Eh? Wasn't there another person?

05:00.280 --> 05:01.740
I was sure I heard two voices.

05:12.750 --> 05:14.340
You've got mail!

05:18.090 --> 05:20.050
I came to deliver a letter.

05:20.680 --> 05:23.760
Are you Ayase Asuna's lover?

05:23.760 --> 05:26.810
E-Eh?! Lover?!

05:26.810 --> 05:30.690
B-But... Ayase!

05:30.690 --> 05:32.100
Are you not?

05:36.230 --> 05:40.990
Well, how would you say it?
Ayase and I don't go to the same school.

05:42.240 --> 05:45.950
But even though we go to different schools...

05:51.540 --> 05:55.080
The two of us first met in this building.

06:01.920 --> 06:05.430
I will now commence propulsion test number one.

06:05.970 --> 06:10.600
Five, four, three, two, one...

06:10.890 --> 06:12.060
Fire!

06:39.550 --> 06:41.710
Experiment failed...

06:54.140 --> 06:58.360
Ever since then, Ayase came regularly to see me test fire my rockets.

06:58.360 --> 07:01.070
Hm, a chance meeting, how nice!

07:01.070 --> 07:02.900
And then? And then?!

07:02.900 --> 07:05.320
But, every visit was hard on me.

07:05.780 --> 07:10.160
No matter how times I explained, she couldn't
understand the workings of the rocket. It was frustrating.

07:10.450 --> 07:12.040
Though that's all right, too.

07:12.620 --> 07:15.000
In other words, a one-sided love.

07:16.920 --> 07:18.920
You don't have to say it so directly...

07:18.920 --> 07:20.090
Well then.

07:21.340 --> 07:23.090
Sorry for the intrusion.

07:23.090 --> 07:23.920
Good day.

07:26.970 --> 07:29.140
Wait, regarding that letter...

07:29.140 --> 07:32.100
Let's say if I were Ayase Asuna's lover, what would have happened?

07:32.100 --> 07:34.770
The letter's author is Ayase Takezou.

07:34.770 --> 07:37.900
Take- Her father? His last words?

07:37.900 --> 07:38.940
Shigofumi.

07:38.940 --> 07:40.560
Shigo...? What did you say?

07:41.230 --> 07:43.900
A letter sent from the world of the departed.

07:44.400 --> 07:46.200
That's why it's called Shigofumi.

07:47.700 --> 07:50.990
The final message left from the person who died.

07:51.580 --> 07:54.250
That's a Shigofumi.

08:05.630 --> 08:09.260
Come on! There's no way someone who died can send a letter, right?

08:09.260 --> 08:12.010
They don't have a body. Do they communicate through mediums?

08:12.010 --> 08:13.810
They do have bodies!

08:14.770 --> 08:17.730
Although we speak of the world of the
dead, it is sorted out into different levels.

08:17.730 --> 08:22.360
Those up to level four have a body, so they can write, and even eat!

08:22.360 --> 08:24.730
The staff... spoke.

08:24.730 --> 08:26.860
I've been talking for a while already!

08:26.860 --> 08:28.860
I can do more than talk, too!

08:30.030 --> 08:31.910
See? I'm standing.

08:31.910 --> 08:32.990
Floating...

08:32.990 --> 08:34.540
I'm standing!

08:34.540 --> 08:37.710
Be quiet, Kanaka. Don't make things complicated.

08:37.710 --> 08:40.580
But, he was talking about mediums and stuff!

08:40.580 --> 08:44.880
You're deviating from both the job and
regulations. Why can't you abide by the rules?

08:44.880 --> 08:46.300
You're a tool, for God's sake.

08:46.300 --> 08:48.170
You're treating me like property again!

08:48.170 --> 08:52.640
I'm not just an Aaron's Rod, I'm partway towards becoming a human!

08:51.550 --> 08:53.390
It can't be. The staff is actually talking.

08:53.390 --> 08:56.100
Ah, enough already! Let's go home!

08:56.100 --> 08:59.690
Ayase Asuna has no lover, recipient unknown!

08:59.690 --> 09:00.100
Yeah.

09:00.480 --> 09:03.940
If there's no one to receive it, then there is nothing we can do.

09:05.230 --> 09:06.610
Shigofumi...

09:07.860 --> 09:08.900
Is it all right?

09:09.240 --> 09:10.150
Is it all right?

09:10.740 --> 09:11.860
Is it all right?

09:12.070 --> 09:12.870
Is it all right?

09:13.570 --> 09:14.580
Sorry.

09:14.870 --> 09:16.120
Wait!

09:22.120 --> 09:24.500
I'll accept that letter.

09:25.540 --> 09:28.550
Hey, didn't you hear what we said?

09:28.550 --> 09:31.260
The letter is addressed to "Ayase Asuna's Lover".

09:31.260 --> 09:34.300
I did! I did, but is it all right?

09:35.140 --> 09:38.680
Is it all right for that letter to not be delivered?

09:39.480 --> 09:43.980
And her father's last words, failing to reach anyone.

09:45.400 --> 09:46.440
That's why...

09:46.900 --> 09:47.860
That's why...

09:47.860 --> 09:48.900
That's why...

09:49.820 --> 09:53.410
I'll become her lover! Then, you won't have any complaints, right?!

09:53.410 --> 09:58.370
Oh! Very good! Very courageous! That's spectacular, young man!

09:58.870 --> 10:03.210
It's love. It's youth. How bittersweet!

10:04.040 --> 10:06.040
Shigofumi

10:07.090 --> 10:09.090
Shigofumi

10:18.310 --> 10:20.100
You don't have to hurry.

10:20.100 --> 10:21.930
Put them in neatly.

10:21.930 --> 10:22.390
Yeah.

10:28.110 --> 10:30.070
Sis, I'm done.

10:30.480 --> 10:33.570
Then seal it with tape. Be sure to write your name, too.

10:33.570 --> 10:34.660
Okay!

10:39.160 --> 10:39.910
Yes?

10:39.910 --> 10:41.790
Ah, um...

10:42.580 --> 10:44.040
Ayase?

10:44.040 --> 10:46.000
Yeah, what's wrong?

10:46.460 --> 10:47.750
Well...

10:48.540 --> 10:50.800
How is it over there?

10:52.880 --> 10:54.180
We're managing.

10:55.010 --> 10:57.850
Er... about your father...

10:58.430 --> 11:00.890
You want to pay your condolences?

11:00.890 --> 11:03.140
There's no need to talk like an adult.

11:03.980 --> 11:06.480
Sorry, I didn't contact you.

11:06.480 --> 11:09.570
There were a lot of processes to go through, so I was very busy.

11:10.070 --> 11:11.360
It's fine.

11:11.650 --> 11:14.400
You're the one who's having it rough.

11:14.400 --> 11:15.240
Well...

11:15.240 --> 11:18.030
No, no. I feel surprisingly fine.

11:18.030 --> 11:20.410
It must be because I'm pretty tough.

11:21.160 --> 11:23.620
Ayase! Is there anything I...

11:22.330 --> 11:23.620
Sis!

11:23.620 --> 11:25.460
Ah, wait one moment.

11:25.460 --> 11:27.330
Leave that one to me.

11:27.330 --> 11:28.130
Yeah.

11:28.580 --> 11:32.340
Sorry, let's talk later again, I'm a bit busy.

11:33.010 --> 11:33.800
See ya.

11:33.800 --> 11:36.300
Wait! I have something important to tell you!

11:36.590 --> 11:37.470
What is it?

11:37.470 --> 11:42.220
That... though this isn't a good time... Actually...

11:42.220 --> 11:43.270
I...

11:43.720 --> 11:44.640
You...?

11:46.270 --> 11:48.020
l-lo-

11:49.940 --> 11:51.070
The rocket!

11:51.360 --> 11:54.360
The rocket is almost done!

11:54.360 --> 11:56.990
Even though you're busy, could you come see it?

11:56.990 --> 11:59.700
I'll wait till you're free, then I will launch it.

12:01.030 --> 12:04.330
I see, your rocket will finally fly.

12:04.330 --> 12:05.620
Sis...

12:05.620 --> 12:06.540
Ah, yeah.

12:07.870 --> 12:12.130
Then give me a message when you've
finished it. I look forward to seeing it.

12:12.130 --> 12:13.840
Ah, okay.

12:13.840 --> 12:14.760
Shouta...

12:14.760 --> 12:15.130
Huh?

12:15.420 --> 12:17.010
Thanks for calling.

12:23.390 --> 12:25.930
Why did you hang up?!

12:25.930 --> 12:28.060
Where's the confession?! Your resolve?!

12:28.060 --> 12:30.520
D-Don't say it like it's something easy!

12:30.520 --> 12:33.110
Confessions require good timing!

12:34.110 --> 12:35.940
You, listen well.

12:35.940 --> 12:40.910
Things like confessions, should be said face to face.

12:40.910 --> 12:43.660
Girls don't like being told by phone, right?

12:43.660 --> 12:44.740
Not really.

12:45.240 --> 12:51.040
You're not thinking that you're going to ride
on the success of your rocket to confess, are you?

12:51.040 --> 12:52.580
Using that rocket.

12:53.090 --> 12:57.550
That's so stupid! If it fails, what will you do!? It'll be bad.

13:01.470 --> 13:08.520
Well, it'd be nice to see both your love and
rocket explode into tiny bits like a firework.

13:08.520 --> 13:10.190
Rockets aren't fireworks!

13:10.190 --> 13:10.640
Yeah, yeah.

13:10.940 --> 13:13.440
It'll launch! I'll show you that it'll definitely succeed.

13:13.440 --> 13:16.440
It'll orbit forever! And so will my love!

13:16.440 --> 13:19.950
Are you trying to sound romantic? Bonded by the rocket's flight?

13:19.950 --> 13:22.610
Sh-Shut it! Staves should keep quiet!

13:22.610 --> 13:24.660
I'm not a staff! I'm Kanaka!

13:24.660 --> 13:27.080
I'm ranked ninth in the Gospel department, you know!

13:26.370 --> 13:28.750
Shut up! Don't be so arrogant when

13:27.620 --> 13:29.580
It seems like this job will take a while.

13:28.750 --> 13:30.370
you engulfed my place in smoke!

13:30.370 --> 13:31.870
That's because of your low quality candles.

13:31.870 --> 13:33.830
Ah! So it <i>was</i> your doing!

13:36.880 --> 13:36.920
Promise

13:36.880 --> 13:36.920
The rocket will
successfully fly!!

14:01.400 --> 14:05.240
Three, two, one. Fuse lit!

14:14.960 --> 14:16.340
Ayase      Asuna

14:16.670 --> 14:19.000
Is this all right?

14:19.000 --> 14:20.550
Yes, thank you.

15:01.090 --> 15:03.090
The rocket will
successfully fly!!

15:03.090 --> 15:05.380
I have to give it a name, I guess.

15:05.380 --> 15:07.640
Hm... Asuna...

15:09.810 --> 15:11.220
Yeah, right!

15:12.060 --> 15:13.850
That's too obvious!

15:13.850 --> 15:17.520
Ah, that's right. She has a sister called Miku. Then...

15:17.520 --> 15:19.360
Why are you talking to yourself?

15:21.780 --> 15:22.780
Where's Kanaka?

15:22.780 --> 15:23.940
Sleeping.

15:24.400 --> 15:25.820
Even though she's a staff?

15:25.820 --> 15:27.740
She's in stand-by mode.

15:28.030 --> 15:30.700
She gets angry if we don't treat her
like a human by not calling it "sleep".

15:31.580 --> 15:32.370
So strange.

15:32.950 --> 15:34.160
So are you.

15:34.160 --> 15:34.870
Huh?

15:34.870 --> 15:38.250
Why did you believe in the Shigofumi?

15:38.710 --> 15:40.420
Normally, people don't.

15:40.880 --> 15:43.760
Because, people didn't believe in me.

15:45.130 --> 15:48.970
"A high school student flying a rocket?" That's so outrageous.

15:48.970 --> 15:49.550
But...

15:51.720 --> 15:53.850
Ayase believed in me.

15:55.100 --> 15:56.640
"That's amazing!", she said.

15:57.480 --> 15:59.940
"I want to see it fly!", she said.

16:00.980 --> 16:06.450
Promise

16:00.980 --> 16:06.450
The rocket will
successfully fly!!

16:01.480 --> 16:04.690
That's why, I tried to believe, too.

16:04.690 --> 16:06.070
So simple.

16:06.900 --> 16:09.030
But, being simple is fine.

16:16.620 --> 16:18.960
Moving tomorrow will be fine, right?

16:18.960 --> 16:20.130
Have you contacted everyone?

16:20.130 --> 16:23.090
I don't have any relatives at school.

16:23.380 --> 16:24.590
How about your friends?

16:27.970 --> 16:30.140
No, it's all right.

16:45.650 --> 16:46.490
Fumika?

16:54.620 --> 16:56.330
When will it be, when will it be?!

16:56.330 --> 17:00.080
It's finally going to come tomorrow, isn't it?! Confession time!

17:00.080 --> 17:00.670
You have bad taste.

17:00.670 --> 17:04.920
What are you saying? You're the one who let him do this.

17:04.920 --> 17:06.000
You're thinking too much.

17:06.000 --> 17:07.880
Don't think I don't know you, partner.

17:07.880 --> 17:10.590
You hate it when letters don't get delivered, right?

17:10.880 --> 17:15.220
I am a professional and take pride in my work, unlike you, Kanaka.

17:15.220 --> 17:16.310
Yeah, yeah.

17:25.020 --> 17:28.150
What's this? There are people living here!

17:28.150 --> 17:31.910
It was worth exploring, huh? There might be other things, too.

17:43.710 --> 17:44.710
Let's go.

17:45.000 --> 17:48.050
W-Wait! Let's investigate more!

17:48.050 --> 17:50.720
Since Shouta needs time alone too.

17:57.600 --> 18:01.730
Sorry, Fumika, I left it at Shouta's place.

18:02.230 --> 18:04.400
It was under the Gospel department's orders.

18:04.900 --> 18:06.190
Fumika?

18:14.490 --> 18:17.120
Shouta, did you read it?

18:18.120 --> 18:21.040
Fumika, what is this?

18:21.370 --> 18:22.960
A Shigofumi.

18:22.960 --> 18:24.670
That's not what I'm asking!

18:25.170 --> 18:27.250
There's a limit to how bad a joke can be!

18:27.250 --> 18:28.340
Ayase...

18:28.920 --> 18:30.550
would never kill her father!

18:31.840 --> 18:35.430
It reads, "The one who killed me was my own daughter, Asuna."

18:35.430 --> 18:38.720
And that her lover should turn her in.

18:38.720 --> 18:40.560
Revenge?

18:40.560 --> 18:42.600
Those who've died cannot lie.

18:42.600 --> 18:44.940
Whether it's kindness, or filled
with hatred, all that is written is true.

18:44.940 --> 18:45.900
Don't fuck with me!

18:46.190 --> 18:47.860
A letter from the world of the departed?

18:47.860 --> 18:49.780
I was an idiot to believe this!

18:59.240 --> 19:00.370
It's a lie...

19:01.620 --> 19:02.830
A lie...

19:03.790 --> 19:05.040
A lie!

19:06.790 --> 19:09.460
Well, then, see you again tomorrow. Bye bye, Miku-chan.

19:11.800 --> 19:13.300
Thank you so much.

19:13.630 --> 19:14.760
Goodbye.

19:22.930 --> 19:24.140
Shouta?

19:34.400 --> 19:36.610
You found my house quite easily.

19:37.070 --> 19:40.160
Because you gave me your address.

19:40.160 --> 19:41.490
Is that so?

19:41.490 --> 19:41.990
Yeah.

19:42.540 --> 19:45.160
That's the first time I've seen your sister.

19:45.160 --> 19:46.250
She's cute.

19:46.250 --> 19:49.750
Yeah. But we're the only ones left.

19:49.750 --> 19:52.710
Since our mother isn't here any more.

19:54.550 --> 19:57.840
It's all right. I've already talked with the people at the city council.

19:57.840 --> 20:00.350
They're putting us in a welfare home.

20:00.890 --> 20:03.810
I'll also be quitting school to go work.

20:04.430 --> 20:07.100
I've been thinking about this for a long time.

20:07.560 --> 20:09.690
About college, dreams and such.

20:09.690 --> 20:12.020
But, when my sister finds something that she wants to do...

20:12.020 --> 20:15.150
I don't want her to give those
things up because we don't have money.

20:16.650 --> 20:21.580
You too, Shouta. Isn't it nice to be able
to put your all into something you enjoy doing?

20:23.200 --> 20:25.700
That's why, I want to do my best for my sister.

20:25.700 --> 20:28.670
<i>No, Ayase can't be the murderer.</i>

20:28.670 --> 20:29.830
<i>She can't be!</i>

20:30.420 --> 20:32.960
Ayase! The rocket is complete!

20:32.960 --> 20:35.920
Eh? Amazing! You did it, Shouta!

20:35.920 --> 20:36.340
Yeah.

20:36.840 --> 20:40.890
If the rocket really does fly, please go out...

20:42.720 --> 20:45.180
Go out with me! Be my girlfriend!

20:46.640 --> 20:48.270
Thank you, Shouta.

20:50.440 --> 20:52.230
But, I'm sorry.

20:52.980 --> 20:54.190
No, it's not like that.

20:54.190 --> 20:57.490
The part about being the student body president too...

20:59.700 --> 21:00.700
Fumika?

21:02.410 --> 21:05.290
Stay away! Ayase didn't do it!

21:05.580 --> 21:08.460
To hell with the Shigofumi! Like I'll believe it!

21:08.460 --> 21:11.000
I'll believe Ayase over that!

21:11.500 --> 21:12.960
The Shigofumi cannot lie-

21:12.960 --> 21:16.840
Shut up! Ayase believed in my rocket.

21:16.840 --> 21:18.840
That's why, I'll believe her!

21:19.170 --> 21:20.510
Let's go, Ayase.

21:20.510 --> 21:22.220
We don't have to deal with this kind of-

21:37.690 --> 21:39.030
Fumika!

21:39.440 --> 21:42.160
Those who are alive lie.

21:42.700 --> 21:46.160
They're weak, scared, ugly.

21:46.620 --> 21:48.870
Those who are dead are much more...

21:53.080 --> 21:57.960
Shigofumi

21:53.080 --> 21:57.960
Episode One

21:53.080 --> 21:57.960
Confession

23:29.100 --> 23:30.560
There were dreams.

23:30.850 --> 23:32.350
There was a future.

23:32.810 --> 23:37.230
What exactly do people seek beyond the azure of the sky?

23:38.440 --> 23:40.440
Next time on Shigofumi:

23:40.860 --> 23:42.150
Rocket.

23:41.230 --> 23:43.230
Shigofumi

23:41.230 --> 23:43.230
Episode Two

23:41.230 --> 23:43.230
Rocket
